        "id": "p69-q6-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $\\angle BOC=2\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p69-q6-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\angle BOC=2\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p69-q6-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use equal base angles in ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\triangle AOB",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and the exterior-angle theorem.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Since $OA=OB$ (radii), $\\angle OBA=\\angle OAB=\\theta$.\n\n$\\angle BOC$ is an exterior angle of $\\triangle AOB$, since $A$, $O$ and $C$ are collinear.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle BOC&=\\angle OAB+\\angle OBA\\\\\\angle BOC&=\\theta+\\theta\\\\\\angle BOC&=2\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q6-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that $AP=1+\\cos 2\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p69-q6-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "AP=1+\\cos 2\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p69-q6-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\triangle OBP",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "OP=\\cos 2\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; add the unit radius ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "AO",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In right-angled $\\triangle OBP$, $\\angle BOP=2\\theta$ and $OB=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos 2\\theta&=\\frac{OP}{OB}\\\\\\cos 2\\theta&=\\frac{OP}{1}\\\\OP&=\\cos 2\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $AO=1$ and $O$ lies between $A$ and $P$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}AP&=AO+OP\\\\AP&=1+\\cos 2\\theta.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      },
      {
        "id": "p69-q6-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Deduce that $\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sin 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p69-q6-c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan\\theta=\\frac{\\sin 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p69-q6-c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "BP=\\sin 2\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\tan\\theta=\\frac{BP}{AP}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "In right-angled $\\triangle OBP$, $OB=1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin 2\\theta&=\\frac{BP}{OB}\\\\\\sin 2\\theta&=\\frac{BP}{1}\\\\BP&=\\sin 2\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\n\nIn right-angled $\\triangle ABP$, use part (b):\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{BP}{AP}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{\\sin 2\\theta}{1+\\cos 2\\theta}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
